<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Italy continues bid to be in first group of EMU.</title>
<headline>Italy continues bid to be in first group of EMU.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy is continuing its efforts to be among the first nations which sign up to European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU), Treasury and Budget Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi said.</p>
<p>For this reason the Italian government would approve the 1997 financial bill, laying out the budget for next year, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Italy is continuing its efforts to be part of the first group of countries entering EMU,&quot; Ciampi told reporters in Dublin where he was attending a meeting of European finance ministers laying out the ground for a future single currency.</p>
</text>
